# WCAG 2.2 Level AA Accessibility

Apply when creating or editing any `.razor` component or scoped CSS.

## Required Patterns

### Buttons & Links
- Icon-only buttons MUST have `aria-label` (localized via `@L["..."]`).
- Toggle buttons MUST have `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`.
- Use `<button type="button">` for non-submit actions.

```razor
<!-- BAD -->
<button @onclick="Toggle"><i class="bi bi-list"></i></button>

<!-- GOOD -->
<button type="button" @onclick="Toggle"
        aria-label="@L["Nav_OpenMenu"]"
        aria-expanded="@(_isOpen.ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
        aria-controls="nav-panel">
    <i class="bi bi-list" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>
```

### Decorative Icons
- Always `aria-hidden="true"` on `<i>` and `<svg>` that are purely visual.
- Meaningful icons need `role="img"` + `aria-label`.

### Images
- Decorative: `alt=""`
- Meaningful: descriptive `alt`, never omit the attribute.

### Forms (SC 1.3.1, 3.3.2, 4.1.3)
- Every input MUST have a `<label for="...">` or `<InputText id="...">` with associated label.
- Error messages: `aria-describedby` pointing to error text, `aria-invalid="true"` on field.
- Hint text: also linked via `aria-describedby`.

```razor
<label for="email">@L["Contact_Email"]</label>
<InputText id="email" @bind-Value="Model.Email"
           aria-required="true"
           aria-describedby="email-err email-hint" />
<span id="email-err" role="alert">@L["Contact_EmailInvalid"]</span>
<span id="email-hint" class="form-text">@L["Contact_EmailPlaceholder"]</span>
```

### Dynamic Content (SC 4.1.3)
- Loading states: `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"`.
- Errors: `role="alert"` (assertive by default).
- Chat/streaming: wrap output region in `aria-live="polite"` `aria-relevant="additions text"`.

### Heading Hierarchy (SC 1.3.1)
- Each page exactly ONE `<h1>`.
- Never skip levels (h1 → h3 is invalid).
- `FocusOnNavigate` already targets `h1` — keep h1 on every page.

### Focus Management (SC 2.4.3, 2.4.7)
- Global `:focus-visible` outline is defined in `app.css` — do NOT remove with `outline: none`.
- Modals/dialogs: trap focus, return focus to trigger on close.
- Skip-link: already in `MainLayout.razor` — keep `#main-content` id on `<main>`.

### Touch Targets (SC 2.5.8 — WCAG 2.2)
- Interactive elements minimum 44x44 CSS pixels.
- Use `min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px;` on icon buttons.

### Motion (SC 2.3.3)
- Wrap non-essential animation in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Existing `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` block in `app.css` — add overrides there.

### sr-only
- Use `.sr-only` utility (defined in `app.css`) for text only screen readers should announce.

```razor
<button @onclick="Save"><i class="bi bi-save" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="sr-only">@L["Tool_Save"]</span></button>
```

### Language
- `<html lang>` is set in `index.html` and toggled by `culture.js`.
- Foreign-language inline content: wrap in `<span lang="en">...</span>`.

## Things to Avoid
- `tabindex` > 0 (positive tabindex breaks DOM order).
- `display: none` on live regions (use `sr-only` instead so AT still announces).
- Relying on color alone to convey state (add icon/text + `aria-*`).
- `outline: none` without a replacement `:focus-visible` style.